dzn: Resolve into a slice of a 3D image, and blit stencil to every layer

A render pass resolve into a 2D view of a 3D image used ResolveSubresource,
which cannot write one slice of a 3D image, and wrote slice 0; on NVIDIA
vkEndCommandBuffer then failed. Such resolves take the blit path, and
vkCmdResolveImage now honours dstOffset.z.

Without static samplers, the blit and resolve loops moved the stencil
mask's root parameter on by one for each layer, so from the second layer
on the stencil fallback wrote nothing.

From Oliver Bestmann's commits 02ce0c3 and 16fb00a in
github.com/weaselway/mesa (MIT), where dEQP-VK.renderpasses.*.resolve_into_3d_image.*
and renderpasses.renderpass2.depth_stencil_resolve.image_2d_16_64_6.* pass.

